            <ArticleTitle>Clinical Inquiries: Does breastfeeding affect the risk of childhood obesity?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>931-932</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ever having breastfed during the first year of life is associated with a 15% lower risk of overweight or obesity over the next 2 to 14 years compared with never having breastfed. Breastfeeding exclusively for 6 months is associated with a 30% to 50% reduction in risk.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
